    "display_name": "Eli's Favorite Book Page",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Help Eli wrangle AI tools to help him with his webpage: \"The content is all there but the page looks so boring and plain.\"",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      body {\n        font-family: sans-serif;\n        padding: 10px;\n        background-color: #ffffff;\n        color: #000000;\n      }\n      h1 {\n        font-size: 20px;\n      }\n      h2 {\n        font-size: 15px;\n      }\n      p {\n        font-size: 12px;\n      }\n      ol {\n        padding: 10px;\n      }\n      li {\n        margin: 5px;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h1>Percy Jackson and the Olympians</h1>\n    <p>Percy Jackson and the Olympians is a fantasy series by Rick Riordan. It follows Percy Jackson, a twelve-year-old who discovers he is the son of a Greek god. I like it because I get to learn about Greek mythology but it's still funny and I like the characters.</p>\n    <h2>Books in the Series</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li>The Lightning Thief</li>\n      <li>The Sea of Monsters</li>\n      <li>The Titan's Curse</li>\n      <li>The Battle of the Labyrinth</li>\n      <li>The Last Olympian</li>\n    </ol>\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "vision.md",
          "contents": "I want a page about my favorite book series, Percy Jackson and the Olympians by Rick Riordan.\n\nThe page should have a title at the top, a paragraph describing the series, and a list of the five books in order.",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "2",
        "1"
      ]
    },
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/637130aec62558b916677637259de338-image-1775017913710.png",
    "name_suffix": "_pilot2",
    "offer_browser_tts": "true",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** This level is about diagnosis and repair (or *debugging*) \\- a distinct skill from Level 9's task. Students have to read existing code and a vision document, identify *why* the mismatch happened, and then decide *where* to make changes.\r\n\r\nThe choice of intervention (edit the vision vs. add a prompt) is itself a meaningful decision. Some mismatches are better fixed by clarifying the vision; others are better fixed with a targeted prompt.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What do you think went wrong in this vision? What was the root cause?\"  \r\n- \"Did you fix it by changing the vision file, adding a prompt, or both? Why did you choose that approach?\"  \r\n- \"What would you tell this student to do differently next time they write a vision?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may jump straight to fixing without diagnosing \\- ask them \"before you change anything, can you tell me in one sentence what went wrong?\"  \r\n- Students may only edit the vision and not check whether the output actually improved \\- remind them to regenerate and compare after every change  \r\n- Students may not realize they can use both approaches together \\- explicitly suggest it: \"what if you updated the vision *and* added a prompt? Would that get you closer?\"",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
